  <!-- Skip Link -->
  <main class="seo-page"><div class="seo-answer"><strong>Direct answer:</strong> Mind Grace Neuropsychiatric Clinic in Greater Noida provides trauma and grief support through counselling and structured therapy, helping individuals and families process loss and traumatic events at their own pace.</div>
<section class="seo-hero"><p class="seo-kicker">Emotional support</p><h1>There is room to talk about loss and difficult experiences</h1><p class="seo-lead">Grief, trauma, and adjustment can affect sleep, mood, relationships, concentration, and the body. Support begins with a conversation at a pace that feels manageable.</p><div class="seo-actions"><a class="btn" href="/therapy/">Explore therapy</a><a class="btn btn-outline" href="/book/">Request an appointment</a></div></section><section class="seo-section"><h2>Possible areas of support</h2><div class="seo-grid"><article class="seo-card"><h3>Making sense of change</h3><p>Talk through what happened, what has changed, and how it is affecting daily life.</p></article><article class="seo-card"><h3>Building steadiness</h3><p>Support may include grounding, routines, coping skills, sleep support, and relationship resources.</p></article><article class="seo-card"><h3>Knowing when to refer</h3><p>Severe symptoms, immediate danger, or specialist needs may require another service or urgent care.</p></article></div><div class="seo-note"><strong>Your pace matters:</strong> No particular therapy method or outcome is guaranteed; suitability is discussed with the clinician.</div></section>    
  </main>
